  "changesObserved": [
    "Library recesses and shelf edges retain depth at the Home and manual orbit views. Window panes show restrained transmitted variation and separate glazing.",
    "Book groups have gaps, occasional supported lean, tooling, more shallow width-dependent spines, and local contact shadows.",
    "Wood stand cap has a planar grain projection instead of the previous swirl; sides use physical height. Walnut and bronze are less orange under the preserved warm light palette.",
    "Three stand silhouettes and material differences remain readable at actual scene scale. Phone view390x844 preserves a single globe and avoids horizontal layout overflow."
  ],
  "remainingVisualWork": [
    "High and close-up images remain stylized; maximum realism has not been achieved.",
    "Balanced and Economy remove bays/rows and make the room too sparse. Next implementation should preserve architectural and book-placement density by using lower-detail compound 3D geometry within existing budgets.",
    "Wood still has visibly procedural elongated grain; bronze wear and leather irregularity are subtle and require further art direction.",
    "The existing common antique light palette and globe halo were preserved, so this review does not establish physically correct complete-room illumination."
  ],
  "validatedBehavior": [
    "One actual scene/camera/globe texture across locale and stand previews",
    "Actual reset and pointer orbit",
    "Library texture allocation returns to the prior actual GPU texture count after preview cancellation"
  ],
